mapping "W3394.1" source="W3394" target="218081007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source W3394 is a Swedish ICD-10-SE extension of base WHO code W33 (Rifle, shotgun and larger
        firearm discharge) with suffixes encoding place (unspecified) and activity (vital activities
        such as rest, sleep, meals, personal hygiene). WHO W33 has Athena SNOMED 218081007 crosswalk to
        SNOMED CT 437167 (Accident caused by firearm missile, concept_code 218081007). The Swedish
        place/activity suffixes have no separate SNOMED CT standard concept; target 437167 fully subsumes
        the clinical firearm-discharge accident event, losing only the SE-specific location/activity
        granularity. Confidence (high): crosswalk-verified standard target with a small, well-understood
        breadth mismatch from the SE extension.
        """
}
